            <div xml:id="d1220">

                <pb facs="0976" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7121.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Winslow to the
                            Secretary of the Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps">San Diego</hi>,” <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Topolobampo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>M–3245. Troop train under General Estrada left Guaymas for Yaqui Valley this
                    morning. General Manso with troop train passed through Hermosillo this morning
                    and is expected in Empalme about noon. General Obregon ordered sixty cars to
                    Hermosillo to carry more troops south; twenty-five of these have already been
                    sent from Empalme. Consul has telegraphed to Esperanza for report of conditions
                    and troop movements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winslow.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
